The characteristics of the rogue level, off the top of my head (apart
from always having a text-terminal-like appearance even on tiled builds)
are:
 * Staircases are visually indistinguishable from one another (although
   still functionally distinct).
 * The level layout is like Rogue rather than like Nethack (with a
   slight tweak because Nethack levels are vertically shorter than Rogue
   levels due to Nethack's larger screen furniture).
 * Doors are opaque but passable terrain.
 * Digging through the wall of a room creates a door, not a doorway.
 * Various types of item have the glyphs they would have in Rogue
   rather than the glyphs they would have in Nethack.
 * Monsters never leave corpses, are generated without inventory, and
   can only be randomly generated if they are of a type represented by
   a capital letter.
 * The game uses Rogue's vision algorithm rather than Nethack's.
